WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.680
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.593
- People may not think pizza
tossing is a serious sport.

00:00:06.593 --> 00:00:09.760
It really is; it's a lot of hard work.

00:00:16.781 --> 00:00:19.374
My name is Tony Gemignani,
and I'm a 12-time

00:00:19.374 --> 00:00:21.894
World Pizza Champion.

00:00:21.894 --> 00:00:23.568
I have two Guinness Book of World Records:

00:00:23.568 --> 00:00:26.915
one for most consecutive
rolls across the shoulders

00:00:26.915 --> 00:00:28.457
in 30 seconds.

00:00:28.457 --> 00:00:30.645
It was 36 rolls across the shoulders,

00:00:30.645 --> 00:00:31.895
36 or 37, yeah.

00:00:32.874 --> 00:00:33.957
We'll say 37.

00:00:35.884 --> 00:00:40.486
So pizza acrobatics are
tricks with pizza dough.

00:00:40.486 --> 00:00:42.283
A lot of people ask me, you know, pizza throwing,

00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:43.981
how do you describe it?

00:00:43.981 --> 00:00:45.725
It's kind of like what a
Harlem Globetrotter does

00:00:45.725 --> 00:00:47.832
with a basketball, but we do with a pizza.

00:00:47.832 --> 00:00:50.045
You know, around the back, across the shoulders,

00:00:50.045 --> 00:00:51.720
through the legs, two at a time,

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.782
on the ground, spinning in your hands.

00:00:54.782 --> 00:00:57.552
The difference between,
you know, a basketball and a pizza

00:00:57.552 --> 00:01:01.118
is it misshapes, it gets
bigger, it gets softer.

00:01:01.118 --> 00:01:02.592
It's not like it's juggling balls

00:01:02.592 --> 00:01:04.339
that are always the same.

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:06.043
It's pretty magical.

00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:09.288
(audience cheers)

00:01:09.288 --> 00:01:11.862
So every year in Las
Vegas, there's Pizza Expo

00:01:11.862 --> 00:01:16.251
and at the Pizza Expo
there's a World Pizza Games.

00:01:16.251 --> 00:01:17.509
When you walk to that stage,

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:20.480
there's acrobats from all
around the world competing.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.172
They'll be getting judged by a panel

00:01:22.172 --> 00:01:23.455
of three to five judges.

00:01:23.455 --> 00:01:26.611
- [Announcer] 8.5, 9.5, nine, nine.

00:01:26.611 --> 00:01:28.415
- And those judges will
look for dexterity,

00:01:28.415 --> 00:01:29.783
creativity, difficulty.

00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:31.403
And as they're judging them,

00:01:31.403 --> 00:01:34.266
they'll look for drops and
they'll look for transitions

00:01:34.266 --> 00:01:35.884
from trick to trick.

00:01:35.884 --> 00:01:37.956
There's about a two to three
minute routine of music,

00:01:37.956 --> 00:01:39.037
they have to nail it.

00:01:39.037 --> 00:01:41.223
They've been practicing all year for it.

00:01:41.223 --> 00:01:43.494
There's a trick in the
sport called the Gemignani,

00:01:43.494 --> 00:01:45.316
my last name, it's a trick that I did.

00:01:45.316 --> 00:01:48.229
It's two across the
shoulders and you catch it.

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:49.923
Nobody loves pizza more than me.

00:01:49.923 --> 00:01:53.447
Even I have it on my
chest, it's pizza for life.

00:01:53.447 --> 00:01:56.280
(audience cheers)

